# Delivery (Fluent Mobile)

## Never push to `main`

**Agents must not** commit, push, or merge directly to `main` (or the default branch).

Every change — including infra, CI, docs, Dependabot follow-ups, and `expo install --fix` — goes through:

1. **Ticket on Project 4** — GitHub Issue `#NNN` **on** the [Fluent Mobile Board](https://github.com/orgs/eten-tech-foundation/projects/4/views/9) (org project #4, view 9). Ask if missing. See [docs/issue-tracking.md](../../docs/issue-tracking.md). The repo Issues list is not the triage board. (Not Linear.) Board Status/Priority edits: [docs/guides/project-board.md](../../docs/guides/project-board.md) and [project-board.mdc](./project-board.mdc) — do not sweep Product or `Dev Ready` lanes without named approval.
2. **Feature branch** — `{author}/{type}/{issue-number}-{slug}` (see `/create-pr-branch`, or `/start-issue` for the full loop)
3. **Pull request** — title `[#NNN]: Description`; body filled from the PR template (below); include `Refs #NNN` under Details (never `Closes` / `Fixes` / `Resolves`); **assign the PR to the author** (`gh pr create --assignee @me` or `gh pr edit --add-assignee @me`); set Project 4 Status to **In PR Review**. Manually link the issue in the PR Development sidebar when needed (GitHub has no non-closing link API — do not use closing keywords). `/start-issue` chains to `/create-pr` (`/open-pr` is an alias) which automates the draft PR, board move, and CI watch.
4. **Human merge** — agents open PRs and push **feature branches only**; never merge on GitHub unless the user explicitly asks for a Dependabot squash merge in that session. For **QA-required** PRs ([docs/guides/qa-process.md](../../docs/guides/qa-process.md)): add `preview-build` and wait for QA pass on **that PR’s** isolated preview — **not mergeable until QA passes**. Project 4 `In QA` is best-effort tracking, not a merge prerequisite. Engineering-only PRs skip that gate. Issues stay open — do not auto-close

Allowed on `main` locally: `git checkout main`, `git pull`, read-only validation after merges. **Not allowed:** `git push origin main`, commits on `main`, or opening PRs with `main` as the head branch.

## PR body (mandatory)

**Every** agent-opened PR body — whether via `/create-pr`, `gh pr create`, or any other path — **must** be filled from [`.cursor/templates/pr-template.md`](../templates/pr-template.md).

Do **not** substitute a short “Summary / Test plan” or ad-hoc bullet list. Load the template and pre-fill:

| Section | Required content |
| ------- | ---------------- |
| **TLDR** | 2–4 sentences: what / why / impact |
| **Reviewer checklist** | Leave items unchecked unless verified |
| **Details** | `Refs #NNN` on its own line (non-closing link); short summary; type-of-change checkboxes |
| **Technical changes** | Key files as `` `path` `` bullets |
| **Testing** | What gates ran (`format:check`, `lint`, `typecheck`, `npm test -- --ci`) or waiver |
| **How to verify** | Numbered steps + **Expected** |
| **Follow-ups** | Deferred AC → linked issues (ticket-level waiver); otherwise say none |

Prefer `/start-issue` (full loop) or `/create-pr` / `/generate-pr-description` so the template is not skipped. Keep under ~400 lines; no nested fenced code blocks inside the PR body.

This repo’s template **wins** over generic personal or org-wide PR body shapes when they conflict.

## Dependabot exception (merge only)

When the user asks to **handle/process Dependabot PRs**, agents may **approve and squash-merge existing Dependabot PR branches** into `main` per [dependabot-workflow.mdc](./dependabot-workflow.mdc). That is merging **their** PRs, not pushing agent-authored commits to `main`.

Agent-authored fixes (expo doctor CI, lockfile repair, conflict resolution) still require a **separate ticketed PR** — never push those straight to `main`.

## Before delivery

Run gates from [commands.mdc](./commands.mdc). Also apply delivery judgment from root [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) (AC, scope, abstraction, human QA) — Cursor pointer: [agent-guardrails.mdc](./agent-guardrails.mdc). Use `/start-issue` for issue → branch → implement → PR, or `/create-pr` when the branch already has commits (template still required if opening the PR another way). See [pr-delivery-ci-gate.mdc](./pr-delivery-ci-gate.mdc).
